    "created_at": "2024-03-03T08:00:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-03-03T08:00:47Z",
    "body": "Wow, this is very surprising for me, thanks for the answer. So I am assuming in all other places where several bytes are prepended at once it is meant to be prepending a sequence?\r\n\r\n* [GB18030 decoder](https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#gb18030-decoder) step 3.1.1.: \"Prepend gb18030 second, gb18030 third, and byte to ioQueue.\"\r\n* [ISO-2022-JP decoder](https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#iso-2022-jp-decoder) step ⤷ Escape 8. : \"prepend *lead* and *byte* to ioQueue\".",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
